INT. FLOODED SUPERMARKET - DAY

Brown water to the waist. Shelves rise like cliffs, stocked with swollen cereal boxes. Sunlight slants through a shattered skylight. A makeshift raft of shopping carts and pallets drifts down the cereal aisle.

LORENZO (40s, soaked, towel on his shoulders) poles the raft with a broom handle. ADEOLA (30s, backpack of canned goods) sits cross-legged, counting cans. KIERAN (15, hoodie, bruised knee) dangles a hand in the water. MRS. OKAFOR-LINDQVIST (70s, cardigan, plastic bonnet) perches on the cart front like a figurehead. PEPPER (12, goggles, plastic sword) stands on a pallet, scanning the shelves.

LORENZO
Left side.

ADEOLA
Left side what?

LORENZO
Aisle's narrowing. Everybody lean.

Everyone leans. The raft slides past a display of cat food. Kieran lifts his hand, and a drowned cardboard banner slaps against his arm. Pepper swings the sword at it, and Mrs. Okafor-Lindqvist ducks, bonnet askew. Adeola catches the can-bag as it tips, Lorenzo plants the pole on a shelf and heaves, and the raft eases into the bread aisle with a long creak.

PEPPER
(to everyone)
Land ho!

MRS. OKAFOR-LINDQVIST
(to Pepper)
Dear, there's no land.

PEPPER
There's a ceiling.

KIERAN
(muttering)
We're going to run out of aisles.

LORENZO
(to Kieran)
Then we'll invent new ones.

ADEOLA
(to herself, counting)
Forty-one, forty-two...

The raft drifts. Sunlight crawls across the water. For a moment nobody speaks.
